 bounded\nunselected component supports. Every actual component is therefore in\nits projected pin tensor space, so both remainder profiles are effective.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.obstruction_decomposition","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.obstruction_decomposition","tooltipHtml":"Subtract the selected scalar atoms supplied by the full obstruction\ndecomposition. The remainder retains full annihilation and bounded\nunselected component supports. Every actual component is therefore in\nits projected pin tensor space, so both remainder profiles are effective."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.rows_of_contraction_zero":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.rows_of_contraction_zero.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.rows_of_contraction_zero:conclusion:Lax342547.EffectiveObstructions.rows_of_contraction_zero:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Every functional annihilating the proposed row space kills each row,\nbecause the corresponding matrix contraction is zero. Coordinate duality\nand double annihilation give membership in the proposed row space.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.rows_of_contraction_zero","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.rows_of_contraction_zero","tooltipHtml":"Every functional annihilating the proposed row space kills each row,\nbecause the corresponding matrix contraction is zero. Coordinate duality\nand double annihilation give membership in the proposed row space."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.sparse_columns":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.sparse_columns.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.sparse_columns:conclusion:Lax342547.EffectiveObstructions.sparse_columns:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Each column of a separated label block keeps its selector row factor.\nReading that column supplies explicit base coefficients on the same labels.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.sparse_columns","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.sparse_columns","tooltipHtml":"Each column of a separated label block keeps its selector row factor.\nReading that column supplies explicit base coefficients on the same labels."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.tensor_of_columns_rows":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.tensor_of_columns_rows.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.tensor_of_columns_rows:conclusion:Lax342547.EffectiveObstructions.tensor_of_columns_rows:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Choose linear retractions onto both factor spaces. Their images of\ncoordinate basis vectors lie in the two factors. The row and column\nconditions reconstruct the matrix as a finite sum of those outer products.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.tensor_of_columns_rows","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.tensor_of_columns_rows","tooltipHtml":"Choose linear retractions onto both factor spaces. Their images of\ncoordinate basis vectors lie in the two factors. The row and column\nconditions reconstruct the matrix as a finite sum of those outer products."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.transpose_blocks":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.transpose_blocks.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.transpose_blocks:conclusion:Lax342547.EffectiveObstructions.transpose_blocks:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Transposition preserves the selector factors and transposes the base\nblock. Commutativity exchanges the two selector scalar factors.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.transpose_blocks","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.transpose_blocks","tooltipHtml":"Transposition preserves the selector factors and transposes the base\nblock. Commutativity exchanges the two selector scalar factors."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.EffectiveObstructions.unselected_tensor":{"href":"../lax-34254